or the  Lockerbie bombing Abdel Basset al  Megrahi  was released by the Scottish government  on compassionate grounds Gordon Brown  denied a deal had been done with the  colonel for the decision angered the  White House when protests over his rule  broke out the Colonel's reaction was  instinctive  ruthless acts of suppression and then as  the rebellion grew absolute defiance  Wow think about the medical love you  could he call those opposing him rats  and vowed to hunt them down  it's street by street house by house and  then gazenga zhang gazenga alleyway to  alleyway ha ha ha  with benghazi about to be overrun a UN  resolution paved the way for  international military intervention when  NATO started bombing they could never  win the ratsy vowed pursue began to  close in on him it took six months and  while NATO bombed foreign forces trained  the rebels eventually they made a  triumphant entry into the capital  Tripoli  that's the sign nothing all makes when  they talk about kakadu 69 year old ex  dictator was reduced to ranting audio  messages in which he insisted he would  prevail the next time a British prime  minister visited Libya  it was the celebrating his part in  Gaddafi's down for David Cameron French  President Nicolas Sarkozy were greeted  his hero pictures and the statues were  hauled down throughout the country for  six weeks the man himself proved elusive  how the people who once lived in terror  of his regime have their final  recognition in woods at Sky News
 

